5 #edb/ref 17592186415059 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415060 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415060 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415060 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186415056 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415060 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f0e50222-5322-5dc6-95c0-87aed25c41a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415061 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186415060 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415061 #edb/ref 1069 "q-35580" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415061 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415061 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is linearly dependent and ${{v}_{1},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is linearly independent, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has only zero solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=0$\n- ${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}$\n- ${v}_{4}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{3}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415061 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0c07b7ca-2c8b-5a74-a857-c6a369e5fb28" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415061 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly dependent set, we obtain that\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nhas a non-zero solution.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, solving equation ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ for ${v}_{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=-\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{2}}{v}_{1}-\\frac{{x}_{3}}{{x}_{2}}{v}_{3}-\\frac{{x}_{4}}{{x}_{2}}{v}_{4}.\n$$\n\nMoreover, ${x}_{2}$ can't be zero because then\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nwill have a non-zero solution and that's a contradiction as ${{v}_{1},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is linearly independent.\nHence, ${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the set ${{v}_{1},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is linearly independent set, the equation \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{3}+{x}_{3}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nhas no non-zero solution. Hence, ${v}_{4}$ is not a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{3}$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415062 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186415063 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415062 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "194a201e-a484-52b1-85fa-bf0a3ff539e0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415062 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186415061 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415063 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186415064 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415063 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "390603f7-3592-5dc2-9f55-cc90d76600ad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415063 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186329740 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415064 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186415066 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415064 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "413d02a4-dfef-5bc6-b884-f744f0683a08" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415064 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186360492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415065 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bca21e33-420e-51ea-b2c1-ea2ef421580a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415065 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407775 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415066 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186415065 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415066 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ccfee361-efb3-56f5-ae8f-8f48353bd1c1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186415066 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186243998 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
